          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>\"The Raven\"</strong><br>\nIn 1845, Poe published \"The Raven,\" a poem that made him famous for its dark and eerie tone and supernatural themes. It is now one of his most famous works, reflecting his fascination with themes of death and loss.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Contributions to Science Fiction</strong><br>\nPoe also contributed significantly to the emerging genre of science fiction with works like \"The Narrative of Arthur Gordon Pym of Nantucket.\" His imaginative and often scientific approach to storytelling paved the way for future authors.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Literary Criticism</strong><br>\nAs a literary critic, Poe was known for his sharp and incisive reviews that often criticized the work of his contemporaries. His analytical skills were evident in his own writing, which showcased his command of language and narrative.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
