            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Struggles and Death</strong><br>\nPoe's life was marked by personal loss, including the death of his wife, Virginia, which had a profound effect on his writing and personal well-being. He struggled with poverty and addiction before his mysterious death in 1849.</p>\n\n<p><strong>\"The Tell-Tale Heart\" and Other Works</strong><br>\nThe Tell-Tale Heart is another of Poe's significant works, exemplifying his skill in conveying psychological depth and terror. His storytelling was unique for its reliability on the internal state of the characters and its intense, dramatic presentation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Poe's Legacy</strong><br>\nPoe's influence on both American and international literature is undeniable. His works are celebrated for their gothic horror and as precursors to modern thrillers. Despite his troubled life, his legacy as a master storyteller endures.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
